==============================================================================
E-S4-2 / E-S4-3  unitarity circle, phase-lag law, spectral dichotomy
==============================================================================
PASS boundary value K(-W^2+i0) == (sqrt(4W^2-1)+i)/(2W)  [derived by limit]
PASS |K|^2 == 1 on the cut, W>1/2 (unitarity circle, exact)
PASS Im K == 1/(2W) == a0/(2 c w)  => phase phi = arcsin(a0/2cw)
PASS Re K == sqrt(1 - 1/(4W^2))  => 1-ReK = 1 - sqrt(1-sin^2 phi)
PASS 2 w Im K == a0/c  (universal secular drift, = laneK)
PASS below edge (W=1/3): Re K == 0 (purely dissipative)
PASS below edge: Im K == (1-sqrt(1-4W^2))/(2W), |K|<1

